<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     OUR STORY
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="story-section">
    <div class="story-inner">
        <div class="story-left">
            <p class="section-label">
                <span class="label-line"></span>
                Our Story
            </p>
            <h2 class="section-title">
                From a <em>Small City</em><br />to a <em>Big Vision</em>
            </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="story-right">
            <p class="story-text">
                In the bustling town of Damak in Eastern Nepal, three ambitious students at Shreeyantra College
                saw a gap in Nepal's procurement ecosystem. Public tenders were opaque, inaccessible, and
                riddled with inefficiency. They envisioned a digital-first platform that would bring fairness,
                speed, and accountability to every government procurement process.
            </p>
            <p class="story-text">
                What started as a college project driven by curiosity and passion quickly transformed into
                the Web Based Public Tender System &mdash; a full-fledged e-procurement platform now serving government agencies and vendors across
                Nepal. Alisha, Ichha, and Arju combined their strengths in leadership, strategy, and technology to
                build something that didn't just solve a problem, but redefined an entire system.
            </p>
            <p class="story-text">
                As young women in the tech space, they became a powerful symbol of women empowerment, proving
                that innovation knows no gender, no age, and no boundary. The Web Based Public Tender
                System is more than a platform &mdash; it's a movement.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


